<core:FragmentDefinition
  xmlns:core="sap.ui.core"
  xmlns="sap.m"
  core:require="{ handler: 'sap/tutorials/admin/missions/ext/TaskColumnHandler' }">
  <!--
    Issue #426 — value-help icon was suppressed in the Path Items LineItem
    table. History: originally the bindings used `%{...}` syntax; that was
    switched to `${...}` (row-context expression binding). But `${...}` alone
    still left the F4 icon missing.

    Real root cause (verified live in the UI5 1.136 runtime): `showValueHelp`
    is a BOOLEAN control property. In a single-reference expression binding,
    UI5 applies the *target property's type* as the referenced part's
    targetType — so it tries to coerce the OData String `taskType` ("TUTORIAL")
    into a boolean BEFORE the expression runs. That throws
      FormatException: "TUTORIAL is not a valid boolean value"
    the binding falls back to `false`, and the icon never renders.

    Fix: opt the string part out of type coercion with `targetType: 'any'`,
    so the expression receives the raw string and evaluates
    `"TUTORIAL" !== 'CHECKPOINT'` → true. A/B tested live: bare `${taskType}`
    → FormatException + showValueHelp:false; `targetType:'any'` →
    showValueHelp:true, no error.

    `editable` below references `IsActiveEntity`, which is genuinely boolean in
    the OData model, so boolean coercion there is a no-op and needs no change.

    Lint guard: test/scripts/check-fragment-binding-mode.test.ts fails if any
    fragment under app/admin/ reintroduces `%{...}` with a row-context
    identifier.
  -->
  <Input
    value="{parts: [{path: 'taskType'}, {path: 'tutorial/title'}, {path: 'group/title'}, {path: 'checkpointTitle'}], formatter: 'handler.formatTaskDisplay'}"
    showValueHelp="{= ${path:'taskType', targetType:'any'} !== 'CHECKPOINT' }"
    valueHelpRequest="handler.onTaskValueHelp"
    editable="{= !${IsActiveEntity} }"
    change="handler.onCheckpointChange"
    placeholder="{path: 'taskType', formatter: 'handler.formatPlaceholder'}"/>
</core:FragmentDefinition>
